tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,app.ui,initNavbar,tabs,scope,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"time\": 1793522149115, \"adjudicated\": 1793529070388},\n{\"claim\": \"Stubbing app/read replies in page tests must match the POST body, not the URL: the record-id discriminator (e.g. id=controls_shared) rides in the POST data, so a URL-only matcher silently passes every request through unstubbed.\", \"detail\": \"Found during peers LOW Phase 1 while stubbing controls_shared/controls_available failures for F16: the correct stub predicate is a match against url + ' ' + postData. This corrects the §3.4 stub recipe in the peers-app-fixes spec, which matched the URL alone and therefore appeared to stub while actually intercepting nothing.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,qa,stubbing,app-read,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793525474520},\n{\"claim\": \"peer.headsup remembers the user's tab pick per peer on the host element: buildControls clicks only ME's own .navbar-tab2, a refresh restores the remembered tab, and only a never-opened peer starts on Dashboard (Phase 1b).\", \"detail\": \"Commit fa4070e4 (peers-app-fixes). The old code clicked document.querySelector('.navbar-tab2') document-wide, yanking every open/refresh to Dashboard and risking a click on some other control's tab bar. The pick is stored on the reused #headsupdisplay host keyed by peer uuid, so it survives the panel's rebuild-on-refresh but resets with the page. The page-scope half of the hazard is still open: the shared app ui initNavbar sweeps 'selected' off every .tab-content under the page root (the Add Connection tabs blank the panel's content) — shared data/app code, deferred to Marc.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,tabs,buildControls,1b\", \"source\": {\"lib\": \"peer\", \"ctl\": \"headsup\", \"facet\": \"js\", \"hash\": \"e7118e6be3f9b4eb\"}, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793532074730},\n{\"claim\": \"The panel's update chips must size to their content: headsup's own .ispos rule made each chip an inline-block stretched to calc(100% - 20px), which clipped the ✓ over the version and stretched the ⚠ chip; the dialog's content-sized chips are the model (Phase 1b).\", \"detail\": \"Commit 90a6539f (peers-app-fixes). Symptom seen in session 2's shots: 'app v123 ➤ 12✓' with the ✓ covering the digits, and '⚠ different author' chips with a wide internal gap. Keep panel chips free of fixed or minimum widths; if a chip misrenders, check headsup's own css overrides before suspecting the shared chip markup that peer.peer's updater builds.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,chips,css,1b\", \"source\": {\"lib\": \"peer\", \"ctl\": \"headsup\", \"facet\": \"css\", \"hash\": \"6f9278b25a6f9d78\"}, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793532078841},\n{\"end\": true}]\n","old":"[\n{\"claim\": \"headsup renders remote-sourced text - result.msg lines, .upgradelist library chips, address chips - with textContent, never innerHTML\", \"detail\": \"F3 (commit a3aa0206), same rule as peer.peer: anything a peer or the network supplies is untrusted. me.update's address chips and the upgrade-list chips are DOM-built with textContent; error msgs are appended as text nodes. The rule applies to every future line touched in this control, not just the F3 spots.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,xss,security,F3\", \"source\": {\"lib\": \"peer\", \"ctl\": \"headsup\", \"facet\": \"js\", \"hash\": \"b7346f6136d1595e\"}, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793417931028},\n{\"claim\": \"#headsupdisplay is one reused container across orb focuses, so state classes set on it (isadmin) leak into the next peer's panel unless reset at mount.\", \"detail\": \"Found on the rig during F7 QA (commit 3a3ae14a, peers-app-fixes): an admin peer's panel earned .isadmin, then a refusing peer's panel opened in the same #headsupdisplay and still showed every admin-only element. The mount handler now strips state classes before wiring. Any future headsup state carried as a class or dataset on the panel root needs the same reset-at-mount discipline.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,ui,mount,state-leak,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793484067319},\n{\"claim\": \"To exercise the HUD panel without driving the 3D scene, mount peer.headsup directly into #headsupdisplay - that is all onSceneFocus does when an orb gains focus.\", \"detail\": \"Used in the F10 panel QA because the scene-host api handle is awkward to reach from a test script; the direct mount runs the identical code path the orb-focus flow runs, so panel behavior (chips, updater, summaries) is fully testable headlessly this way.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,testing,qa,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"time\": 1793485879002},\n{\"claim\": \"Stubbing peer data for HUD tests must drive #headsupdisplay's api directly - wrapping the json() global never intercepts the panel's 10s poll\", \"detail\": \"The panel's periodic peer re-read calls the closure-scoped send_peers binding, not the json global, so a json() stub is bypassed. Working recipe: mutate the orb's live DATA record (e.g. set address:'' and remote_address) and call document.getElementById('headsupdisplay').api.update() - that api object IS the panel's me. Restore the record afterwards. Found while testing F13's remote_address fallback.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,qa,testing,stub,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793518275981},\n{\"claim\": \"The .hideme utility class cannot hide the HUD's round buttons on its own: the shared app css declares .roundbutton-small { display: inline-flex } after .hideme at equal specificity, so .hideme's display:none loses the cascade — hiding such a button needs a more specific rule (headsup now carries .hudpanel .closeaddressbutton.hideme { display:none }).\", \"detail\": \"Root cause of the F13 stray ✕ (fixed in commit cd43ddeb, journal patch p43): the close-address button was never actually hidden by .hideme; it merely sat invisible under the ⋯ button while .abspos stacked them, and became visible the moment Phase 4 removed .abspos. The expand/collapse click handlers set inline style.display, which outranks the new rule, so toggling still works. General lesson: any element combining .hideme with a class the app css later gives an explicit display value will render; check computed style, not class lists.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,css,hideme,roundbutton,cascade,specificity,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793521886147},\n{\"claim\": \"Scripted instant close-then-reopen of the peer HUD races the close animation: the close's async onfinish fires after the reopen and stamps display:none onto the hud, blanking the fresh panel — a test-harness artifact, not a product bug.\", \"detail\": \"Hit during Phase 5b step-4 verification (close panel, immediately reopen via hostData.onFocus). Real users cannot trigger it: the 300ms close animation finishes before an orb can be re-tapped, and watchHud guards. Test scripts driving the HUD must either wait out the close animation before reopening or restore display after the stale onfinish lands.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,testing,animation,race,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793521892425},\n{\"claim\": \"Pixel sampling proves only that the expected content is present — it cannot reveal the unexpected. When screenshots cannot be viewed, every control in the photographed region must also be checked for visibility (getComputedStyle display, getBoundingClientRect), not just the elements the test case names.\", \"detail\": \"Phase 5 of peers-app-fixes marked M22 PASS while its own collapsed shot showed a stray orange ✕ (a Phase 4 regression): the sampler counted the pixels the case expected and had no way to notice an extra button. The 5b fix (cd43ddeb) was only found by a human viewing the image. Standing QA rule for this rig: enumerate the interactive elements in the shot region and assert each one's computed visibility matches the state being photographed.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,qa,screenshots,pixel-sampling,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793522133686},\n{\"claim\": \"Evidence screenshots must be produced by real user actions with the window visible (document.hidden false); states manufactured by directly toggling classes or styles photograph UI no user can reach. For tabbed UI, assert the tab header and the content agree (.navbar-tab1.selected together with .tab1.selected) before shooting.\", \"detail\": \"The Phase 5b m22 retakes were taken while document.hidden with the Info CONTENT forced visible by script after buildControls had auto-switched the panel header to Dashboard — a header/content combination no in-page click can produce (initNavbar toggles both sides synchronously). The byte-identical files were the tell. Phase 6 retook them with the window visible, Info clicked as a user, and both selected-class pairs verified in agreement. Related quirk: agent.browser.act refuses navbar-tab divs as 'disabled' (same as <tr> rows) — use the plain click tool.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,qa,screenshots,document.hidden,tabs,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793522141739},\n{\"claim\": \"The headsup panel's tabs are not isolated from the page's: app ui initNavbar clears 'selected' from every .tab-content under its el scope, so clicking the Add Connection dialog's LAN/Connect tabs (page scope) blanks the panel's content while its header stays highlighted; and buildControls in peer.headsup clicks document.querySelector('.navbar-tab2') document-wide, auto-yanking every fresh panel to Dashboard.\", \"detail\": \"Measured on the rig (MEDIUM Phase 6, 2026-11-01): with the panel on Info, Add Connection → Connect left navbar-tab1 selected but .tab1 content stripped (display none) — a real-user header/content mismatch; master has the same code. The full fix (scoping initNavbar's content sweep to the tabs' own container) is a shared app change for Marc; the buildControls lookup could be scoped to ME in peer.headsup. Filed in 3-LOW.md 'To check'. Any control that mounts tabbed sub-controls inside a tabbed page inherits this hazard.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,peer.peer,app.ui,initNavbar,tabs,scope,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793522149115},\n{\"end\": true}]\n","patch_id":"p51","time":1793532082924},{"author":"claude","facet":"js","label":"6b: NOT FOUND renders through buildControls like any empty list","new":"    if (result.status == 'ok'){\n      me.data = result.data;\n      buildControls();\n    }\n    else if (result.msg == 'NOT FOUND'){\n      // 6b (Marc): 'NOT FOUND' is the default state — this peer has never\n      // shared a control — not an error. Render it through buildControls\n      // like any other empty list, so both empty cases show the same note\n      // and open on the same tab. F11: Add Control stays enabled.\n      me.data = { \"list\": [] };\n      buildControls();\n    }\n    else {\n      // F16: failures show the shared wording (errText), as text (F3).\n      ME.querySelector('.hudapps').textContent = errText(result);\n      me.data = { \"list\": [] };\n      // F11: a failed read makes adding unsafe (a write would replace a\n      // list we never saw), so the menu item goes dark with the reason.\n      disableAddControl(errText(result));\n    }","old":"    if (result.status != 'ok'){\n      // F16: failures show the shared wording (errText), as text (F3).\n      // 'NOT FOUND' is not a failure — the peer has never shared a\n      // control — so the dashboard stays empty instead of naming an error.\n      ME.querySelector('.hudapps').textContent = result.msg == 'NOT FOUND' ? '' : errText(result);\n      me.data = { \"list\": [] };\n      // F11: 'NOT FOUND' only means this peer has never shared a control.\n      // Any OTHER failure makes adding unsafe (a write would replace a list\n      // we never saw), so the menu item goes dark with the reason on it.\n      if (result.msg != 'NOT FOUND') disableAddControl(errText(result));\n    }\n    else {\n      me.data = result.data;\n      buildControls();\n    }","patch_id":"p52","time":1793537653495},{"author":"claude","facet":"js","label":"6b: a dim note (plus an admin-only hint) on an empty dashboard","new":"  var data = me.data;\n  var wrap = ME.querySelector('.hudapps');\n  wrap.innerHTML = '';\n\n  // 6b (Marc): an empty dashboard is the default state, not an error — say\n  // so instead of leaving the tab blank. The peer's name is peer-reported:\n  // textContent, never innerHTML (F3). The hint only helps someone who can\n  // use the menu, so it carries .adminonly and F7's .isadmin rule decides\n  // whether it shows.\n  var list = data && data.list ? data.list : [];\n  if (list.length == 0){\n    var note = document.createElement('div');\n    note.className = 'hudapps-empty';\n    note.textContent = (ME.DATA.name || 'This peer') + \" hasn't shared any controls yet.\";\n    var hint = document.createElement('div');\n    hint.className = 'adminonly';\n    hint.textContent = 'Add one with ⋮ → Add Control.';\n    note.appendChild(hint);\n    wrap.appendChild(note);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  for (var i in data.list){","old":"  var data = me.data;\n  var wrap = ME.querySelector('.hudapps');\n  wrap.innerHTML = '';\n\n  for (var i in data.list){","patch_id":"p53","time":1793537661663},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"6b: dim style for the empty-dashboard note","new":"/* 6b: the empty-dashboard note (Marc: 'NOT FOUND' is the default state,\n   not an error). Dim; the admin hint inside it inherits the dimming and\n   F7's .adminonly/.isadmin rule decides whether it shows at all. */\n.hudpanel .hudapps-empty {\n  opacity: 0.55;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  padding: 12px 0;\n}\n\n/* F8: the save-failure words next to Stay connected */","old":"/* F8: the save-failure words next to Stay connected */","patch_id":"p54","time":1793537668391},{"author":"claude (peers-app-fixes phase 7)","facet":"html","label":"7.3: one header row (✕ · name/UUID · dots · ⋮) on the inner gutter","new":"<div class='hudheader'>\n  <img src='../app/asset/app/icons/ui/dark/close.svg' class='closehud roundbutton-small-white'>\n  <div class='rp-info hudtitle'>\n    <div class='headline rp-name'></div>\n    <div class='rp-uuid'></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class='hudheadright'>\n    <div class='rp-info hudconn'>\n      <div class=\"connectionindicator\"></div><div class=\"connectionindicator\"></div><div class=\"connectionindicator\"></div>\n      <div class='connectionlatency'></div>\n    </div>\n    <img src='../app/asset/app/icons/ui/dark/more-vertical.svg' class='roundbutton-small-white popupmenu morebutton' data-popup='{\"selector\":\".control-settings-popup\",\"closeselector\":\".control-settings-popup-close\",\"popup\":true}'>\n    <div class='card popupcard mini control-settings-popup'>\n      <table class=\"tablelist\">\n        <tr><td class=\"refreshhud closeonclick\">Refresh</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"adminonly popupmenu closeonclick\" data-popup='{\"selector\":\".add-control-popup\",\"closeselector\":\".add-control-popup-close\",\"modal\":true}'>Add Control</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"adminonly closeonclick\">Control Settings</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"hudrestart adminonly closeonclick\">Restart Services</td></tr>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"navbar-dark\">\n  <div class=\"navbar-tab navbar-tab1 selected\" data-id='tab1'>Info</div>\n  <div class=\"navbar-tab navbar-tab2\" data-id='tab2'>Dashboard</div>\n</div>","old":"<div class='top-right'>\n  <div class='rp-info'>\n    <div class=\"connectionindicator\"></div><div class=\"connectionindicator\"></div><div class=\"connectionindicator\"></div>\n    <div class='connectionlatency'></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class='card popupcard mini control-settings-popup'>\n    <table class=\"tablelist\">\n      <tr><td class=\"refreshhud closeonclick\">Refresh</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"adminonly popupmenu closeonclick\" data-popup='{\"selector\":\".add-control-popup\",\"closeselector\":\".add-control-popup-close\",\"modal\":true}'>Add Control</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"adminonly closeonclick\">Control Settings</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"hudrestart adminonly closeonclick\">Restart Services</td></tr>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n  <img src='../app/asset/app/icons/ui/dark/more-vertical.svg' class='roundbutton-small-white popupmenu morebutton' data-popup='{\"selector\":\".control-settings-popup\",\"closeselector\":\".control-settings-popup-close\",\"popup\":true}'>\n</div>\n<div class='padme'>\n  <img src='../app/asset/app/icons/ui/dark/close.svg' class='closehud roundbutton-small-white marginme'>\n  <div class='rp-info'>\n    <div class='headline rp-name'></div>\n    <div class='rp-uuid'></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class = \"navbar-dark\">\n    <div class = \"navbar-tab navbar-tab1 selected\" data-id='tab1'>Info</div>\n    <div class = \"navbar-tab navbar-tab2\" data-id='tab2'>Dashboard</div>\n  </div>","patch_id":"p55","time":1793539696097},{"author":"claude (peers-app-fixes phase 7)","facet":"html","label":"7.3: drop the closer of the removed wrapping .padme","new":"    <div class='card-text'>\n      <div class = 'add-control-available'></div>\n      <div class='add-control-error'></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>","old":"    <div class='card-text'>\n      <div class = 'add-control-available'></div>\n      <div class='add-control-error'></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","patch_id":"p56","time":1793539701841},{"author":"claude (peers-app-fixes phase 7)","facet":"css","label":"7.3: header row + shared inner gutter rules","new":"/* 7.3: ONE inner gutter for the whole panel — the header, the tab bar\n   and both tab bodies start at the same x (the tab bodies' .padme is\n   24px, so the gutter is 24). */\n.hudpanel {\n  --hud-gutter: 24px;\n}\n\n/* 7.3: one header row: ✕ and the name share a vertical centre (bo