anel's update chips must size to their content: headsup's own .ispos rule made each chip an inline-block stretched to calc(100% - 20px), which clipped the ✓ over the version and stretched the ⚠ chip; the dialog's content-sized chips are the model (Phase 1b).\", \"detail\": \"Commit 90a6539f (peers-app-fixes). Symptom seen in session 2's shots: 'app v123 ➤ 12✓' with the ✓ covering the digits, and '⚠ different author' chips with a wide internal gap. Keep panel chips free of fixed or minimum widths; if a chip misrenders, check headsup's own css overrides before suspecting the shared chip markup that peer.peer's updater builds.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,chips,css,1b\", \"source\": {\"lib\": \"peer\", \"ctl\": \"headsup\", \"facet\": \"css\", \"hash\": \"6f9278b25a6f9d78\"}, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793532078841},\n{\"claim\": \"The panel's layout contract (Phase 7): one .hudheader flex row (✕ · name/UUID · dots+latency · ⋮) and a .hudinfogrid two-column grid share one inner gutter (--hud-gutter, 24px = the tab bodies' .padme), and the admin-only Platform block joins the grid via display:contents.\", \"detail\": \"Commits 3dd81fbf + 982443e8 (peers-app-fixes). ✕ and the name both sit on the 32px name line (shared vertical centre); the UUID sits under the name at the name's left edge; the ⋮ menu card anchors in .hudheadright (position:relative). Grid: labels (and the key/lock icons, glyphs pulled back 6px) in column 1 at x24, values in column 2 at x136; .hudinfofull spans both columns (address list, crate form/status, Stay connected). .hudpanel.isadmin .hudcrates{display:contents} must stay AFTER the .isadmin .adminonly revert rule (equal specificity, source order decides), and initCrates' remove() of .hudcrates still drops all its grid rows at once. Empty Info values render '—' (js), the key row's failed check says 'unknown', and the ⋯ carries title 'Show all addresses (N)' with a dim +N beside the IP when the peer reported more than one. Don't re-wrap the 