nous width loops and frame-separated width steps both relaid out correctly, because any forced layout read heals the stale tracks; only a real pointer drag's cadence triggered it. Verification recipe: take the live screenshot, navigate the driven tab to it via file:// (a chrome-privileged goto may leave http for file:), draw it on a canvas, band-profile the panel region per row (text/accent/mid pixel counts), and compare band edges with the recorded getBoundingClientRect values — they must agree within antialiasing noise.\", \"tags\": \"peer.headsup,qa,testing,screenshot,paint,rects,phase7c\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793543741953},\n{\"end\": true}]\n","patch_id":"p73","time":1793613908681},{"author":"claude (peers-dashboard D1)","facet":"html","label":"D1: open the pinned .hudtop block around the header","new":"<div class='hudtop'>\n<div class='hudheader'>\n  <img src='../app/asset/app/icons/ui/dark/close.svg' class='closehud roundbutton-small-white'>","old":"<div class='hudheader'>\n  <img src='../app/asset/app/icons/ui/dark/close.svg' class='closehud roundbutton-small-white'>","patch_id":"p74","time":1793877163006},{"author":"claude (peers-dashboard D1)","facet":"html","label":"D1: close .hudtop after the panel's tab bar","new":"  <div class=\"navbar-tab navbar-tab2\" data-id='tab2'>Dashboard</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n","old":"  <div class=\"navbar-tab navbar-tab2\" data-id='tab2'>Dashboard</div>\n</div>\n","patch_id":"p75","time":1793877171929},{"author":"claude (peers-dashboard D1)","facet":"css","label":"D1: header + tabs pinned together; tile navbars static in the panel","new":".hudpanel > .hudtop > .navbar-dark {\n  width: auto;\n  margin: 0 var(--hud-gutter);\n}\n\n/* D1: the header and the tab bar are ONE pinned block. The kit's navbar\n   rule (app.ui) is sticky at top:61px — the height of an app title bar\n   this panel doesn't have — so inside the panel (#headsupdisplay, the\n   scroll container) the tab bar floated 61px down with content showing\n   through the gap. .hudtop sticks at the top instead, on the panel's own\n   solid ground (D3), and the tab bar inside it is static. z-index 10:\n   above tile content (whose navbars are static below), under the kit's\n   popup cards (15+), so the Add Control and camera modals still open on\n   top. */\n.hudpanel > .hudtop {\n  position: sticky;\n  top: 0;\n  z-index: 10;\n  background-color: var(--panel);\n}\n\n.hudpanel > .hudtop > .navbar-dark {\n  position: static;\n  background-color: transparent;\n}\n\n/* D1: tab bars that dashboard controls bring (the camera tile's\n   LIVE/DVR/EVENTS) scroll with their tile while they're in the panel.\n   Scoped to .hudapps, so those controls' own pages keep the kit's\n   sticky bar. */\n.hudpanel .hudapps .navbar,\n.hudpanel .hudapps .navbar-dark,\n.hudpanel .hudapps .navbar-light,\n.hudpanel .hudapps .navbar-accent {\n  position: static;\n}","old":".hudpanel > .navbar-dark {\n  width: auto;\n  margin: 0 var(--hud-gutter);\n}","patch_id":"p76","time":1793877208335},{"author":"claude (peers-dashboard D2)","facet":"css","label":"D2: dots on the name line, latency centred under them, glyphs flush with the tab bar","new":"/* D2: the dots' box IS the three dots (a flex row, no line box around\n   them), so .hudheadright's align-items centres the dots themselves on\n   the name row — the latency used to ride in that box and lift the dots\n   6px above the line. The latency hangs under the dots, out of flow,\n   centred on them. */\n.hudheader .hudconn {\n  position: relative;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 3px;\n}\n\n.hudheader .connectionindicator {\n  margin: 0;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\n.hudheader .connectionlatency {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 100%;\n  left: 50%;\n  transform: translateX(-50%);\n  margin-top: 3px;\n  text-align: center;\n  white-space: nowrap;\n  line-height: 1;\n}\n\n/* D2: the ✕ and ⋮ glyphs sit flush with the tab bar's edges. Both are\n   32px buttons (6px padding, 24-unit icon drawn in 20px); the glyphs'\n   own insets differ: the ✕ strokes start 5.125 units in (round caps),\n   the ⋮ dots end 10.125 units short of the right. Pull each box out by\n   padding + its glyph inset, so the hover circle may overhang the\n   gutter but the glyph lands on it. */\n.hudheader .closehud {\n  margin-left: calc(-6px - 20px * 5.125 / 24);\n}\n\n.hudheader .morebutton {\n  margin-right: calc(-6px - 20px * 10.125 / 24);\n}","old":".hudconn {\n  text-align: right;\n}\n\n.hudheader .connectionindicator {\n  margin-top: 0;\n}","patch_id":"p77","time":1793877218894},{"author":"claude (peers-dashboard D2)","facet":"css","label":"D2: keep the dots at their 12px size","new":".hudheader .connectionindicator {\n  margin: 0;\n}","old":".hudheader .connectionindicator {\n  margin: 0;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}","patch_id":"p78","time":1793877339446},{"author":"claude (peers-dashboard D1)","facet":"css","label":"D1: pinned block under the modal backdrop","new":"   solid ground (D3), and the tab bar inside it is static. z-index 4:\n   above tile content (whose navbars are static below), and UNDER the\n   kit's modal backdrop (.greyedout, 5) and popup cards (15+) — so the\n   Add Control and camera modals open on top and the backdrop covers the\n   header too (no header click leaks past an open modal). The ⋮ menu\n   card lives inside this block and paints at its level. */\n.hudpanel > .hudtop {\n  position: sticky;\n  top: 0;\n  z-index: 4;","old":"   solid ground (D3), and the tab bar inside it is static. z-index 10:\n   above tile content (whose navbars are static below), under the kit's\n   popup cards (15+), so the Add Control and camera modals still open on\n   top. */\n.hudpanel > .hudtop {\n  position: sticky;\n  top: 0;\n  z-index: 10;","patch_id":"p79","time":1793877505296},{"author":"claude (peers-dashboard D2)","facet":"css","label":"D2: the header name ellipsizes instead of wrapping","new":"/* D2: a long peer name ellipsizes on its one 32px line (it used to wrap\n   and push the UUID down) — the same rule as the UUID. */\n.hudtitle .rp-name,\n.hudtitle .rp-uuid {\n  overflow: hidden;","old":".hudtitle .rp-uuid {\n  overflow: hidden;","patch_id":"p80","time":1793877596503},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"headsup: tab bar keeps its strip background (Phase 1 review)","new":"/* Phase 1 review: static only — the bar keeps the kit's own strip\n   (.navbar-dark's --panel-2), like every other tab bar in the app. */\n.hudpanel > .hudtop > .navbar-dark {\n  position: static;\n}","old":".hudpanel > .hudtop > .navbar-dark {\n  position: static;\n  background-color: transparent;\n}","patch_id":"p81","time":1793878365205},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"headsup: ⋮ card without the kit margin (Phase 1 review)","new":"/* Phase 1 review: app.ui opens this card position:fixed with an inline\n   left/top at the click point (clamped to innerWidth - offsetWidth - 10),\n   so right/top here never applied — the kit's .popupcard margin:20px did,\n   pushing the card 20px past that clamp (10px out of the window). No\n   margin; the ⋮ click handler in the js lines the card's right edge up\n   with the tab bar's. */\n.hudpanel .control-settings-popup {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.control-settings-popup {\n  position:absolute;\n  width:300px;","old":".control-settings-popup {\n  position:absolute;\n  right:-20px;\n  top:6px;\n  width:300px;","patch_id":"p82","time":1793878370961},{"author":"claude","facet":"js","label":"headsup: ⋮ card's right edge on the tab bar's (Phase 1 review)","new":"  document.body.api.ui.initPopups(ME);\n  // Phase 1 review: app.ui puts the ⋮ card at the click point, clamped\n  // 10px inside the window, which lands it off the panel's grid. This\n  // listener runs after initPopups' (same element, added later), so the\n  // card is open and measurable: its right edge goes on the tab bar's\n  // right edge, its top just under the ⋮.\n  ME.querySelector('.morebutton').addEventListener('click', function(){\n    var card = ME.querySelector('.control-settings-popup');\n    if (card.style.display == 'none') return;\n    var bar = ME.querySelector('.hudtop > .navbar-dark').getBoundingClientRect();\n    card.style.left = (bar.right - card.offsetWidth) + 'px';\n    card.style.top = (this.getBoundingClientRect().bottom + 4) + 'px';\n  });\n  initCrates();","old":"  document.body.api.ui.initPopups(ME);\n  initCrates();","patch_id":"p83","time":1793878375093},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"headsup: dashboard tiles in order, big rows, wrapping icons, one gap (D4)","new":"/* D4: the dashboard is one wrapping row of tiles, in the list's order,\n   with ONE gap (--hud-tile-gap) between tiles and between rows; the tab\n   body's .padme already puts it on the gutter. A big tile takes a whole\n   row at the panel's inner width, so it breaks the row before and after\n   it; consecutive icon tiles share rows, left-aligned. The old inline\n   flow put small tiles wherever it could, and a big tile held a fixed\n   600x450 box whatever its content. */\n.hudpanel {\n  --hud-tile-gap: 16px;\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudapps {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  align-items: flex-start;\n  gap: var(--hud-tile-gap);\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudapps-empty {\n  flex: 1 0 100%;\n}\n\n/* D4: a big tile's height follows its content, from a 16:9 minimum of\n   its width. The minimum is needed: camera:dvr sizes itself FROM its\n   slot (adjustSizes fits the image into the slot's height minus its own\n   navbar), so an auto-height slot would collapse it to nothing. 16:9 is\n   the camera's default resolution, so its image fills the row's width;\n   content taller than that grows the slot (aspect-ratio's automatic\n   minimum is the content). */\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtile.big {\n  flex: 0 0 100%;\n  min-width: 0;\n  height: auto;\n  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;\n}\n\n/* D4: an icon tile is a fixed square (peer:reboot draws its canvas from\n   the slot's size once, at ready). */\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtile.iconmode {\n  flex: none;\n  width: 150px;\n  height: 150px;\n}","old":".inline.big{\n  width:600px;\n  height:450px;\n  /* 7b: the panel is resizable down to 360px — a big dashboard tile\n     caps at the panel's inner width instead of holding 600px. */\n  max-width:100%;\n}\n\n.inline.iconmode{\n  width:150px;\n  height:150px;\n}","patch_id":"p84","time":1793878698887},{"author":"claude","facet":"js","label":"headsup: tiles carry .hudtile (D4)","new":"    var el = document.createElement('div');\n    // D4: .hudtile carries the dashboard layout (css); big/iconmode stay\n    // for any control that reads its slot's mode.\n    el.className = 'inline hudtile ' + claz;","old":"    var el = document.createElement('div');\n    el.className = 'inline ' + claz;","patch_id":"p85","time":1793878701485},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"headsup: dashboard is a size container (D4)","new":".hudpanel .hudapps {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  align-items: flex-start;\n  gap: var(--hud-tile-gap);\n  container-type: inline-size;   /* cqw = the dashboard's inner width */\n}","old":".hudpanel .hudapps {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  align-items: flex-start;\n  gap: var(--hud-tile-gap);\n}","patch_id":"p86","time":1793878873194},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"headsup: big tile 16:9 minimum, grows with content, overflow stays in slot (D4)","new":"   the camera's default resolution, so its image fills the row's width;\n   in-flow content taller than that grows the slot (height:auto above a\n   min-height — not aspect-ratio, whose grow-with-content minimum is\n   lost on a scroll container). overflow-y:auto keeps what a tile paints\n   OUTSIDE its own boxes inside its slot: at a 360px panel the camera's\n   DVR tab fits its controls into the slot by shrinking its image to 0\n   and spilling the rest (391px into 176) over the next tile. That is\n   the camera's own layout (session 3); here it scrolls in its slot. */\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtile.big {\n  flex: 0 0 100%;\n  min-width: 0;\n  height: auto;\n  min-height: calc(100cqw * 9 / 16);\n  overflow-y: auto;\n}","old":"   the camera's default resolution, so its image fills the row's width;\n   content taller than that grows the slot (aspect-ratio's automatic\n   minimum is the content). */\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtile.big {\n  flex: 0 0 100%;\n  min-width: 0;\n  height: auto;\n  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;\n}","patch_id":"p87","time":1793878883578},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"headsup: tile gap 12px, two icons per row at the 360px minimum (D4)","new":"/* 12px: the header's own gap, and two 150px icon tiles + one gap fill\n   the 312px inner width of a panel at its 360px minimum exactly. */\n.hudpanel {\n  --hud-tile-gap: 12px;\n}","old":".hudpanel {\n  --hud-tile-gap: 16px;\n}","patch_id":"p88","time":1793878978365},{"author":"claude","facet":"html","label":"D5: Edit/Done button on the DASHBOARD tab","new":"  <div class='padme tab-content tab2'>\n    <div class='hudeditbar adminonly'>\n      <span class='hudedit-msg' role='status'></span>\n      <button type='button' class='regularbutton hudeditbutton' aria-pressed='false'>Edit</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class='hudapps'></div>","old":"  <div class='padme tab-content tab2'>\n    <div class='hudapps'></div>","patch_id":"p89","time":1793879419212},{"author":"claude","facet":"js","label":"D5: edit mode — reorder and remove tiles with fresh-read writes","new":"    // D5: the tile's slot (el) sits in a wrapper that is the flex item and\n    // the positioned box for the edit overlay — installControl replaces\n    // el's children, so the overlay can't live inside el. The wrapper\n    // records the tile's index and type, which edit writes check against\n    // the fresh list.\n    var tw = document.createElement('div');\n    tw.className = 'hudtilewrap ' + claz;\n    tw.dataset.index = i;\n    tw.dataset.type = ctl.type;\n    var el = document.createElement('div');\n    // D4: .hudtile carries the dashboard layout (css); big/iconmode stay\n    // for any control that reads its slot's mode.\n    el.className = 'inline hudtile ' + claz;\n    tw.appendChild(el);\n    wrap.appendChild(tw);\n    d.peer = ME.DATA.id;\n    installControl(el, db, id, function(api){}, d);\n  }\n  decorateTiles();\n}\n\n// D5: edit mode. Each tile gets an overlay (it swallows clicks, so a tile's\n// own buttons — Reboot — can't be pressed while editing) with a bar of\n// real buttons: ← → ✕. ✕ asks first, inline in the same bar. Titles and\n// the peer name are peer-reported: textContent and setAttribute only (F3).\nfunction tileButton(text, label, cls, fn){\n  var b = document.createElement('button');\n  b.type = 'button';\n  b.className = 'hudtile-btn' + (cls ? ' ' + cls : '');\n  b.textContent = text;\n  b.title = label;\n  b.setAttribute('aria-label', label);\n  b.addEventListener('click', function(e){ e.stopPropagation(); fn(); });\n  return b;\n}\n\nfunction tileTitle(idx, type){\n  var it = me.data && me.data.list ? me.data.list[idx] : null;\n  return it && it.title ? String(it.title) : String(type);\n}\n\nfunction showMoveBar(bar, idx, type, n){\n  var title = tileTitle(idx, type);\n  bar.textContent = '';\n  var left = tileButton('←', 'Move ' + title + ' earlier', '', function(){\n    editWrite(idx, type, function(l){ l.splice(idx - 1, 0, l.splice(idx, 1)[0]); });\n  });\n  left.disabled = idx == 0;\n  var right = tileButton('→', 'Move ' + title + ' later', '', function(){\n    editWrite(idx, type, function(l){ l.splice(idx + 1, 0, l.splice(idx, 1)[0]); });\n  });\n  right.disabled = idx == n - 1;\n  var gap = document.createElement('span');\n  gap.className = 'hudtile-gap';\n  var x = tileButton('✕', 'Remove ' + title, 'hudtile-remove', function(){ showConfirm(bar, idx, type, n); });\n  bar.appendChild(left);\n  bar.appendChild(right);\n  bar.appendChild(gap);\n  bar.appendChild(x);\n}\n\nfunction showConfirm(bar, idx, type, n){\n  var title = tileTitle(idx, type);\n  bar.textContent = '';\n  var q = document.createElement('span');\n  q.className = 'hudtile-q';\n  q.textContent = 'Remove ' + title + ' from ' + (ME.DATA.name || 'this peer') + \"'s dashboard?\";\n  bar.appendChild(q);\n  bar.appendChild(tileButton('Remove', 'Remove ' + title, 'hudtile-remove', function(){\n    editWrite(idx, type, function(l){ l.splice(idx, 1); });\n  }));\n  var cancel = tileButton('Cancel', 'Keep ' + title, '', function(){ showMoveBar(bar, idx, type, n); });\n  bar.appendChild(cancel);\n  cancel.focus();\n}\n\nfunction decorateTiles(){\n  ME.querySelectorAll('.hudapps .hudtile-edit').forEach(function(o){ o.remove(); });\n  if (!me.editing) return;\n  var tiles = ME.querySelectorAll('.hudapps > .hudtilewrap');\n  tiles.forEach(function(tw){\n    var ov = document.createElement('div');\n    ov.className = 'hudtile-edit';\n    var bar = document.createElement('div');\n    bar.className = 'hudtile-bar';\n    ov.appendChild(bar);\n    tw.appendChild(ov);\n    showMoveBar(bar, Number(tw.dataset.index), tw.dataset.type, tiles.length);\n  });\n}\n\n// D5 (the F11 rule): never write a list we haven't just seen. Re-read\n// controls_shared, check the tile is still the one the user pointed at\n// (index AND type), apply the change to the FRESH list, write it back.\n// A moved-under-us list writes nothing and rebuilds; a failed read or\n// write says why beside Edit and leaves the dashboard as it was.\nfunction editWrite(idx, type, mutate){\n  var msg = ME.querySelector('.hudedit-msg');\n  msg.textContent = '';\n  ME.querySelectorAll('.hudapps .hudtile-edit button, .hudeditbutton').forEach(function(b){ b.disabled = true; });\n  function settle(){\n    ME.querySelector('.hudeditbutton').disabled = false;\n    decorateTiles();\n  }\n  json('../peer/remote/'+ME.DATA.id+'/app/read', \"lib=runtime&id=controls_shared\", function(rr){\n    var fresh;\n    if (rr.status == 'ok') fresh = rr.data && rr.data.list ? rr.data : { \"list\": [] };\n    else if (rr.msg == 'NOT FOUND') fresh = { \"list\": [] };\n    else { msg.textContent = errText(rr); settle(); return; }\n    var it = fresh.list[idx];\n    if (!it || it.type != type) {\n      me.data = fresh;\n      ME.querySelector('.hudeditbutton').disabled = false;\n      buildControls();\n      msg.textContent = 'The dashboard changed. Refreshed it; try again.';\n      return;\n    }\n    mutate(fresh.list);\n    json('../peer/remote/'+ME.DATA.id+'/app/write', \"lib=runtime&id=controls_shared&readers=[]&writers=[]&data=\"+encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(fresh)), function(result){\n      if (result.status != 'ok') { msg.textContent = errText(result); settle(); return; }\n      me.data = fresh;\n      ME.querySelector('.hudeditbutton').disabled = false;\n      buildControls();\n    });\n  });\n}\n\nME.querySelector('.hudeditbutton').addEventListener('click', function(){\n  me.editing = !me.editing;\n  this.textContent = me.editing ? 'Done' : 'Edit';\n  this.setAttribute('aria-pressed', me.editing ? 'true' : 'false');\n  ME.querySelector('.hudedit-msg').textContent = '';\n  decorateTiles();\n});","old":"    var el = document.createElement('div');\n    // D4: .hudtile carries the dashboard layout (css); big/iconmode stay\n    // for any control that reads its slot's mode.\n    el.className = 'inline hudtile ' + claz;\n    wrap.appendChild(el);\n    d.peer = ME.DATA.id;\n    installControl(el, db, id, function(api){}, d);\n  }\n}","patch_id":"p90","time":1793879438600},{"author":"claude","facet":"js","label":"D5: Edit goes dark when the dashboard can't be read","new":"      disableAddControl(errText(result));\n      // D5: same reason — no edit can be checked against a list we can't read\n      var eb = ME.querySelector('.hudeditbutton');\n      eb.disabled = true;\n      eb.title = 'Editing is unavailable: ' + errText(result);\n    }\n  });","old":"      disableAddControl(errText(result));\n    }\n  });","patch_id":"p91","time":1793879444136},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"D5: tile wrapper is the flex item","new":".hudpanel .hudapps > .hudapps-empty {\n  flex: 1 0 100%;\n}\n\n/* D5: the flex item is the tile's wrapper (.hudtilewrap); the slot the\n   control mounts in (.hudtile) fills it. The wrapper is the positioned\n   box the edit overlay covers. */\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtilewrap {\n  position: relative;\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtilewrap.big {\n  flex: 0 0 100%;\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtilewrap.iconmode {\n  flex: none;\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudtilewrap > .hudtile {\n  display: block;\n}","old":".hudpanel .hudapps > .hudapps-empty {\n  flex: 1 0 100%;\n}","patch_id":"p92","time":1793879447735},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"D5: big slot rules move under the wrapper","new":".hudpanel .hudtilewrap > .hudtile.big {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: auto;","old":".hudpanel .hudapps > .hudtile.big {\n  flex: 0 0 100%;\n  min-width: 0;\n  height: auto;","patch_id":"p93","time":1793879452364},{"author":"claude","facet":"css","label":"D5: edit overlay, tile bar and Edit row styles","new":".hudpanel .hudtilewrap > .hudtile.iconmode {\n  width: 150px;\n  height: 150px;\n}\n\n/* D5: edit mode. The overlay covers the whole tile and takes every click\n   (so Reboot can't be pressed by mistake); it sits under the pinned\n   header block (z-index 4). The bar rides the tile's top edge. */\n.hudpanel .hudtile-edit {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n  z-index: 3;\n  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);\n  outline: 1px dashed var(--text-dim);\n  outline-offset: -1px;\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudtile-bar {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 6px;\n  padding: 6px;\n  background: var(--panel-2);\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudtile-gap {\n  flex: 1;\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudtile-q {\n  flex: 1 0 100%;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  line-height: 16px;\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n}\n\n.hudpanel .hudtile-btn {\n  min-width: 28px;\n  height: 28px;\n  padding: 0 8px;\n  font: inherit;\n  font-size: 14px;\n